      "content": "That feeling of performing while feeling completely hollow is exhausting, and it's a very painful place to be. When you feel like you've already finished, it suggests the effort of keeping up is far outweighing any reward. You don't have to keep performing for anyone; sometimes the kindest thing you can do is give yourself permission to stop the act. A simple, quiet moment of letting go of expectations might be the first small step toward finding a different kind of peace.",
